<title>BELGIUM: Tractebel deal to net Royale Belge 4 bln bfr.</title>
<headline>Tractebel deal to net Royale Belge 4 bln bfr.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Insurer Royale Belge said on Tuesday it would book a four billion franc capital gain from the sale of its stake in energy and engineering holding company Tractebel to Belgium's biggest holding firm Societe Generale de Belgique.</p>
<p>&quot;At the price of 14,500 Belgian francs per share, the transaction will bring in a total of 8.2 billion and allow Royale Belge to realise a capital gain of nearly four billion,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>It added that the money would be used to develop its core business of financial services.</p>
<p>-- Newsroom +32 2 287 6810.</p>
